  "id": "cognitive-electrophysiology",
  "term": "cognitive electrophysiology",
  "definition": "Cognitive electrophysiology is the study of brain electrical activity in relation to cognitive tasks or mental processes, typically using signals such as EEG. In this context, it refers to using neurophysiological recordings alongside other information to understand or screen for differences linked to cognition and neurodevelopment.",
